#BRUTEFORCE APPROACH

Key Idea
For each index i, traverse the entire array.
Skip nums[i].
Multiply all other elements.
Store the product in ans[i].
Repeat for every index.

TIME : O(N^2)
SPACE: 0(1) 

CODE:->>

class Solution {
    public int[] productExceptSelf(int[] nums) {
        int ans[] = new int[nums.length];

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            int product = 1;
            for(int j = 0; j < nums.length; j++) {
                if(i != j) {
                    product *= nums[j];
                }
                ans[i] = product;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}



#OPTIMIZED APPROACH (prefix and suffix)

Key Idea
Use prefix product and suffix product.
For each index i:
answer[i] = product of all elements before i × product of all elements after i
Calculate prefix products in one pass and suffix products in another.

Time: O(n)
Extra Space: O(1) excluding the output array.

CODE:->>

class Solution {
    public int[] productExceptSelf(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] ans = new int[n];

        // Prefix product
        int prefix = 1;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            ans[i] = prefix;
            prefix *= nums[i];
        }

        // Suffix product
        int suffix = 1;
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            ans[i] *= suffix;
            suffix *= nums[i];
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
